    {
      "id": "5WGSr3DbIRAA0JbUXQ2rc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 327,
      "y": 126.5,
      "width": 1024.0592041015625,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "btd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1693364076,
      "version": 153,
      "versionNonce": 1943757268,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786839715841,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Design a single-node, embeddable key–value store library with a simple API that must remain correct\nand durable across process crashes and power failures.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Design a single-node, embeddable key–value store library with a simple API that must remain correct and durable across process crashes and power failures.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fiZaRHFmRhxEOcHiKIYFq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 328.40625,
      "y": 196.3046875,
      "width": 287.57989501953125,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bte",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1043709164,
      "version": 59,
      "versionNonce": 374813420,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786840058039,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** HIGH LEVEL DESIGN ***",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** HIGH LEVEL DESIGN ***",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xBI-HFc-vXUawUF48AfUu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 327,
      "y": 233.5,
      "width": 995.831298828125,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "btf",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1925930196,
      "version": 1361,
      "versionNonce": 1228592212,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786841231044,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Build an LSM-tree (Log-structured merge) embeddable KV store.\n- Stated constraint (SSD/NVMe, crash+power-loss durability), every durable write is sequential append\n- The store will have 5 moving parts:\n1) WAL -- every mutation appended and fsync'd before it is acked. \n2) Memtable -- in-memory sorted structure holding recent writes, keep consistent with WAL\n3) SSTables -- immutable, sorted on-disked files produced by flushing full memtable, never modified in\nplace\n4) Manifest + CURRENT -- crash-safe metadata describing which SSTables are live, level they sit at,\nlast durable sequence number\n5) Compaction -- background process merge SSTables, drops shadowed versions and tombstones,\nbound read/space amplication\n\nTo make thing crash-safe\n1) Nothing is acked until it's in fsync'd WAL record: recovery rebuild in-memory state by replaying WAL\n2) On-disk files installed atomically: file fully written + fsync'd to temp name, then live by `rename`\nor by manifest/CURRENT swap",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Build an LSM-tree (Log-structured merge) embeddable KV store.\n- Stated constraint (SSD/NVMe, crash+power-loss durability), every durable write is sequential append\n- The store will have 5 moving parts:\n1) WAL -- every mutation appended and fsync'd before it is acked. \n2) Memtable -- in-memory sorted structure holding recent writes, keep consistent with WAL\n3) SSTables -- immutable, sorted on-disked files produced by flushing full memtable, never modified in place\n4) Manifest + CURRENT -- crash-safe metadata describing which SSTables are live, level they sit at, last durable sequence number\n5) Compaction -- background process merge SSTables, drops shadowed versions and tombstones, bound read/space amplication\n\nTo make thing crash-safe\n1) Nothing is acked until it's in fsync'd WAL record: recovery rebuild in-memory state by replaying WAL\n2) On-disk files installed atomically: file fully written + fsync'd to temp name, then live by `rename` or by manifest/CURRENT swap",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
